    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0240" n="220" xml:id="pg220"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690B.9321/4–2354: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 161<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Thailand (Parsons) to the
                        Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d161-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-23T17:00:00+07:00">April 23, 1954—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2146. Thai representative joint committee today gave first indication Thai
                    willingness participate evacuation south group suggesting committee receive
                    evacuees Burma, impound arms Thai side border when operation begins. Foreign
                    Office awaiting committee recommendations, expects government will approve
                    provided safety guarantees sufficient. Burmese extended ceasefire Palu area
                    through 30 April requesting Foreign Forces refrain from attacks on GUB forces
                    from area. GUB still considering Myawadi safety corridor request.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d161-f2"/> Approval would facilitate committee action.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d161-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Parsons</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d161-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d161-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Taipei and Rangoon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d161-f2" n="2" xml:id="d161-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 2128 from Bangkok, Apr. 21, reported that, following a Joint Committee
                    inquiry, the Burmese Ambassador requested his government to consider
                    establishing a safety corridor from Palu through Myawadi. (690B.9321/4–2154)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d161-f3" n="3" xml:id="d161-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram 2158 from Bangkok, Apr. 27, reported that the Burmese Government
                    approved the Committee’s proposal on Apr. 27 with the provision that the
                    evacuation begin by May 5 and finish by May 15. (690B.9321/4–2754)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
